Wood-effect vinyl tile is an alternative to parquet with considerable advantages. This tile is produced using a particular photographic printing technology. That is what makes it possible to recreate a natural, one-of-a-kind wood pattern. On top of that, embossing achieves the characteristic relief, which is hard to tell from the real thing.

Another advantage of wood-effect vinyl floor tile is the polyvinyl chloride in the covering. It is exactly what makes the floor warm and pleasant to walk on barefoot, even in the cold months. This tile is widely used for floors in buildings where floor temperature particularly matters — gymnasiums, sports complexes and children's facilities.

